  "id": "Compound::DB00402 - Gene::2561",
  "verbalization": "Eszopiclone is implicated in the regulation of Gabrb2 through a series of molecular interactions involving Zopiclone. The evidence suggests that Eszopiclone, through its effects on Alcohol Intoxication, Dysosmia, and Retrograde Amnesia, is linked to Zopiclone, which binds to Gabrb2. This binding is supported by multiple paths, all of which share a common pathway involving Zopiclone as the lowest common ancestor. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores indicates a consistent relationship between Eszopiclone and Gabrb2, likely through the intermediary of Zopiclone. The mechanisms involve the modulation of neural activity, possibly through the GABA receptor system, which is a well-established target for sedative-hypnotic drugs. The evidence supports a functional link between Eszopiclone and Gabrb2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
